%N A398829 Numbers k having at least two distinct prime factors and the property that p + 10 divides k + 10 for all primes p dividing k.
%D A398829 Jean-Marie De Koninck, Ces nombres qui nous fascinent, Entry 50, p. 19, Ellipses, Paris 2008.
%H A398829 Michael S. Branicky, <a href="/A398829/b398829.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..300</a>
%p A398829 isOk := proc(n, d:=10) local f,i; f := ifactors(n)[2]; if nops(f) < 2 then return false fi; for i from 1 to nops(f) do: if irem(n + d, f[i][1] + d) > 0 then return false fi: od: return true: end:
%o A398829 (PARI) d=10; isok(n) = my(f=factor(n)); if(#f~ < 2, return(0)); for(i=1,#f~,if((n + d)%(f[i,1]+d) != 0,return(0))); 1
%o A398829 (Python)
%o A398829 from sympy import factorint
%o A398829 def ok(n): return len(f:=factorint(n)) > 1 and all((n+10)%(p+10) == 0 for p in f)
%o A398829 print([k for k in range(10**6) if ok(k)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Sep 12 2026
%Y A398829 Subsequence of A024619.
%K A398829 nonn,new
